WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.809 --> 00:00:05.017
- We were the smallest town for a while.

00:00:05.017 --> 00:00:07.000
Do we still wish we were?

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.553
I don't know, to be a population of one

00:00:09.553 --> 00:00:12.256
and a population of two, and
you're both in the same county,

00:00:12.256 --> 00:00:13.661
in the same state.

00:00:13.661 --> 00:00:16.328
I think that's pretty wonderful.

00:00:18.885 --> 00:00:21.988
- [Man] What is the population of Monowi?

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:23.938
- Population one,

00:00:23.938 --> 00:00:24.771
me.

00:00:26.639 --> 00:00:29.606
- The population of Gross,
Nebraska is one, two.

00:00:29.606 --> 00:00:30.439
One, two.

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:33.590
- [Elsie] We don't have enough people.

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:36.196
It's nothing against the
towns, nothing against the

00:00:36.196 --> 00:00:37.476
people running the businesses.

00:00:37.476 --> 00:00:41.546
We simply have run out of
people out in this area.

00:00:41.546 --> 00:00:44.409
- [Mary] All we have in
town is the bank vault

00:00:44.409 --> 00:00:46.549
that remains from the Gross State Bank.

00:00:46.549 --> 00:00:48.368
Then we have a community Hall.

00:00:48.368 --> 00:00:52.946
And then our house and the
trailer house across the street.

00:00:52.946 --> 00:00:54.263
- We had a high school here.

00:00:54.263 --> 00:00:58.013
There was church until,
oh, maybe the mid '60s.

00:00:58.907 --> 00:01:01.541
- We have the same paperwork
and everything to fill out

00:01:01.541 --> 00:01:04.876
that Omaha and New York City
and every other city has.

00:01:04.876 --> 00:01:06.620
We don't have an election for mayor,

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:08.926
I just let him keep that job.

00:01:08.926 --> 00:01:11.176
(laughing)

00:01:14.975 --> 00:01:16.356
- [Elsie] The young folks or any

00:01:16.356 --> 00:01:18.017
that go from here to the city,

00:01:18.017 --> 00:01:20.640
they can adjust pretty well
and make a good life there,

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:23.242
but you take somebody that's
born and raised in the city

00:01:23.242 --> 00:01:28.047
and they usually just can't
hack it out in this area.

00:01:28.047 --> 00:01:30.265
- [Mary] Never gets lonely
living in a town of two.

00:01:30.265 --> 00:01:32.543
There's always somebody passing through.

00:01:32.543 --> 00:01:34.008
Values are different.

00:01:34.008 --> 00:01:36.286
You don't have everything
at your fingertips,

00:01:36.286 --> 00:01:39.869
so you just learn to
sit and converse more.

00:01:43.817 --> 00:01:45.707
- I'm not here because I have to be.

00:01:45.707 --> 00:01:47.673
I could close up and
leave here any time I wanted,

00:01:47.673 --> 00:01:49.454
go wherever I wanted.

00:01:49.454 --> 00:01:52.454
I'm here because I want to be here.

